{"checkedAt": "2026-11-14T10:27:19.874125+00:00", "documents": [{"sha256": "74a8332a2d29cc2792511843b4eee26e759f5798371df8f567eebf3ef49a6c4f", "sourceUrl": "https://www.lseg.com/content/dam/ftse-russell/en_us/documents/ground-rules/russell-us-indexes-construction-and-methodology.pdf", "version": "v7.4, November2026"}, {"sha256": "d9e4c50186666664257890de5a5c8cf9f7f52cc135a1eda85f8469e94733e266", "sourceUrl": "https://www.lseg.com/content/dam/ftse-russell/en_us/documents/other/russell-index-calculation-methodology.pdf", "version": "v1.2, September2026"}], "originalWeightsUnchanged": true, "rule": "Equity-member weights use the same closing float-adjusted market values across the standard Russell2000 price/gross/net return series. Withholding tax changes the dividend return calculation, not these market values. Only equity weights are referenced; RU20INTR returns never replace RU20N30U returns. Hedged, capped, style and leveraged variants are excluded.", "targetReturnSeriesUnchanged": true}